    "title": "Lu Dort regrets hip-checking Nikola Jokic - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Hanifan ,\n5 hours ago (GIF courtesy of GIPHY // Oklahoma City Thunder) Lu Dort regrets hip-checking Nikola Jokic The Oklahoma City Thunder have been the NBA’s best defense for two years. Although, at times, their physicality and aggression defensively becomes a little too much.\nSpecifically, from one particular player: Lu Dort\nIn a nationally-televised meeting between the reigning-champion Thunder and Denver Nuggets, Dort and superstar Nikola Jokic got into a spat in the fourth quarter, with Dort haphazardly hip-checking the three-time MVP after a made free-throw attempt.\nDort, who’s been labeled a dirty player by many, expressed his regret to reporters recently.\n“Obviously, that was unnecessary contact that I shouldn’t have done,” he said, according to The Athletic’s Joel Lorenzi. “I got the worst of it by getting thrown out the game. But yeah, it was a high-level game. I’m a competitor, so I compete.\n“That’s a physical game and there’s limits to it. And I went over the limit. … “(The incident) has nothing to do with going against that team. We love going against that team. It’s always a nice matchup whenever we play against them. And it’s fun.”\nIn the same vein, Dort also claimed he wasn’t a “dirty” player. It was a chippy game between two conference rivals who expect to compete for an NBA Title. However, this specific act was dirty by Dort; it was completely unnecessary and malicious … and it looked fairly intentional.\nDort was ejected as a result of the action, while the shoving match between Jokic and Thunder center Jaylin Williams resulted in nothing for either player.\nThis wasn’t the first incident that the seventh-year vet’s been involved in, either. Earlier this season, he was in another shoving match with Pelicans rookie Jeremiah Fears , who’s temper has also run hot on a few different occassions.\nThese 3 teams fulfill the 40-20 rule in 2025-26 Dort hasn’t been afraid to be ultra-physical with many of league’s top ballhandlers. He’s one of the best defensive players in the NBA — but he oftentimes takes it over the top without any retribution. In this case, there was — and rightfully so.\n***\nClick Here for more NBA Content\nSubscribe to Vendetta’s Twitch\nSubscribe to Vendetta’s YouTube\nCheck out the Vendetta Shop\nCheck out Vendetta Fantasy Contests\nThe post Lu Dort regrets hip-checking Nikola Jokic appeared first on Vendetta Sports Media .",
